cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Navigator's Log — Research Integrity (commit-before-run + frozen-instrument-scaffold)"
abstract: >-
  An installable Claude Code plugin packaging a trustworthy pre-run discipline for
  empirical ML / AI-safety research. commit-before-run generates a hash-pinned
  preregistration with a freeze block and refuses to certify a run until the
  decision rule, content-matched control, publish-either-way null, and cheapest
  replication are committed; it also grows via an append-only lessons ledger.
  frozen-instrument-scaffold provides a "carry a frozen probe to a model it was
  never fit to" transfer harness with the confound-control ladder and known traps
  pre-guarded.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Head
    given-names: Christopher Blake
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-2308-6051"
    affiliation: "Navigator's Log R&D"
